[notes]
- Software-only C01 preprocessing fit; product card C01 remains not_run; no model training, no causal replay windows, no verify_data entrypoint, no online scene.
- Only train split members were decompressed for fitting; held-out members were cross-checked at manifest level only and never opened.
- PF01 repair: numeric conversion now happens only for depth (index 0) and the four selected channel columns; every other column is validated for cardinality and structural line shape but never parsed numerically. Labels/confidence/coordinates may contain opaque nonnumeric sentinels without affecting stats; malformed selected/depth values still fail with member+line.
- PF02 repair: supplied split tables are now validated for unique row_id/well_id, inventory member-sha and UWI identity, derived root equality, declared counts and root purity via read-only data/grouping.py:validate_split_assignments before any fitting; shared-parent-across-splits and wrong-well_id fixtures are rejected.
- Stats regeneration equals the pre-repair snapshot (bitwise channels, train block, fitting members and row totals) as captured by the compare run against C:\Users\Alan\Documents\ChatGPT\FPGA\CarlandFPGA-node-c\.local\plan-20261014-final-c\director-startup\preprocess-before-repair1\data\preprocessing.json.
- preprocessing.json is regenerated per run; only generated_utc differs between runs (same byte length), all fitted numbers identical.
- The earlier repair capture used a readback script whose 'grouping root purity enforced' check was vacuous ('or True'); the final readback2 recomputes identity and root purity independently, and this final capture is the cited evidence.
